-- #1619 CONTROL — main.mdk's entry with the colliding module removed from the
-- import graph, and NOTHING else changed. `other.mdk` is still on disk (the
-- loader walks imports, so a module nobody imports is not in the graph), so the
-- ONE dimension that flips is whether the same-spelled interface is present.
--
-- Without it, `dtag Box` reaches di's inherited default and answers 7 — which is
-- exactly the half of the correct pair that main.mdk loses. If this file also
-- stopped answering 7, cross-module interface DEFAULTS would be broken in
-- general and #1619's framing would be wrong; the harness then says
-- CONTROL-BROKE rather than DRAINED.
--
-- Per #1144 a control is graded on its EXIT CODE ONLY, so it ASSERTS 7 and
-- panics otherwise rather than printing it — a control that merely printed would
-- exit 0 either way and could never fail. PROVEN ABLE TO FAIL: changing the
-- comparand to a value the program cannot produce, 77, makes `medaka run
-- control.mdk` exit 1 with `runtime error [E-PANIC]: control regressed: ...`
-- (measured 2026-08-14, then reverted).
import dimpl.{Box(..), dtag}

main =
  if dtag Box == 7
    then println "control-ok:7"
    else panic "control regressed: the inherited cross-module default no longer answers 7"
